1
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:09,820
<i>Due to heavy rain, the next train is running
 about twenty minutes behind.</i>

2
00:00:10,390 --> 00:00:14,950
<i>We sincerely apologize for the 
delay in service today.</i>

3
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,810
I-I'm sorry!

4
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:20,880
It's okay.

5
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:25,410
The train sure is late, huh?

6
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:28,750
Yeah. I'm getting sleepy just waiting.

7
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:33,450
<i>But I'm glad she's still here with me.</i>

8
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:38,840
<i>Today, we kissed for the first time.</i>

9
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,900
<i>This... isn't a dream, is it?</i>

10
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:04,040
<i>If I could tell my old self that 
we'd really fall in love,</i>

11
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,590
<i>I wonder how I'd react.</i>

12
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:49,390
Episode 12

13
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:49,390
My First Love

14
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,610
Whoa! Here. Here!

15
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:50,060
Let me guess. 
Do you have a crush on that girl?

16
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:52,300
Huh?

17
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:55,870
You've been watching her this 
whole time, haven't you?

18
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,050
Hit it higher!

19
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:00,480
I see now.

20
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:05,530
No wonder you keep coming out here 
in the cold. That explains it.

21
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:10,430
N-No, you're wrong! I don't really... 
have a crush on her.

22
00:03:10,750 --> 00:03:16,310
She just picked up something 
for me I dropped the other day.

23
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:17,760
Hmm...

24
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:19,770
Sorry!

25
00:03:19,770 --> 00:03:20,770
It's okay, it's okay!

26
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,580
Goodness.

27
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:23,760
Excuse me!

28
00:03:25,090 --> 00:03:28,000
Just be careful not to hit 
it into the road, okay?

29
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,380
All right. Thank you very much.

30
00:03:31,890 --> 00:03:33,900
A Boy's Chair

31
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:38,440
Thanks for waiting!

32
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,810
Now that's one nice girl.

33
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,910
Sorry!

34
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:42,370
Really? She just seems normal to me.

35
00:03:42,370 --> 00:03:44,940
You sure don't get it, youngster.

36
00:03:45,230 --> 00:03:48,120
It's normal to help people in need.

37
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:51,540
If you do something wrong, 
it's normal to apologize.

38
00:03:52,060 --> 00:03:53,580
Remember to say thank you.

39
00:03:54,320 --> 00:04:00,110
But it's actually pretty difficult 
to do "normal" things all the time.

40
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,590
I'm home.

41
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:10,860
Listen, Saki is just about to graduate.

42
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,110
He studied so hard for his entrance exam.

43
00:04:14,110 --> 00:04:16,100
You should come home for a while.

44
00:04:16,890 --> 00:04:19,860
Oh, Saki-kun. Welcome home.

45
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:19,860
Oh dear. Are you really going to say that?

46
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,650
Thank you, Auntie.

47
00:04:22,170 --> 00:04:25,180
Is that my mom on the phone?

48
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:28,930
Um, well, yes. But they're having 
a bit of an argument.

49
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:32,160
I'm not sure you'll get to talk to her today.

50
00:04:33,770 --> 00:04:35,540
Ah! There, there!

51
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:39,220
For goodness sake!
He's your son, you stubborn fool!

52
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:46,270
Welcome home, Saki.

53
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:48,090
Thank you.

54
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,910
I can't find that monster anywhere!

55
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,010
Oh, I just saw him.

56
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:00,550
Really? Where is he?

57
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:01,400
Here, here.

58
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:06,170
Did you hear? Yao-kun asked 
a girl in class 2 out!

59
00:05:06,170 --> 00:05:08,540
Wow! He's got guts!

60
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:13,060
And then you know what?

61
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:12,490
Um... We still have cleaning to do.

62
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:19,050
<i>I guess she doesn't like interrupting 
when people are talking.</i>

63
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:22,160
<i>I can kind of relate.</i>

64
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:27,720
<i>But why do I keep thinking 
about her so much?</i>

65
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:35,690
The book I just borrowed 
is really interesting!

66
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:37,940
A Boy's Chair

67
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:37,430
Oh? What kind of book is it?

68
00:05:42,950 --> 00:05:45,600
<i>What in the world am I doing?</i>

69
00:05:57,450 --> 00:06:00,910
<i>Was she too shy to talk 
to that lady at first?</i>

70
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:07,380
<i>It's actually pretty difficult 
to do "normal" things all the time.</i>

71
00:06:10,970 --> 00:06:13,460
You're all going to be graduating soon.

72
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:17,490
So today, I'd like to give 
you a special assignment.

73
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:19,480
Feb.14th

74
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:19,480
PE

75
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:19,480
Japanese

76
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:19,480
Math

